{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s42-p01",
      "text": "A red sky at sunset may mean that there are clear skies to the west, where the sun sets.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p02",
      "text": "A red sky at sunrise usually means that the clear weather has already passed, so storms might be coming.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p03",
      "text": "Forecasting the weather has been practiced for thousands of years.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p04",
      "text": "In the 5th century BC, the Greeks sent out forecasts to sailors.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p05",
      "text": "They used signs in nature to forecast the weather.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p06",
      "text": "But today, meteorologists provide exact forecasts further in advance.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p07",
      "text": "They use scientific instruments to study weather conditions around the world and make forecasts.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p08",
      "text": "Pilots, farmers and many other people depend on these forecasts.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p09",
      "text": "Luckily, most of us can simply check the smartphone or turn on the TV to find out what kind of weather is coming.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p10",
      "text": "If you are looking for some signs of the weather, pay attention to nature.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p11",
      "text": "There are two basic rules used in weather forecasting.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p12",
      "text": "Weather generally moves from west to east.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p13",
      "text": "And low air pressure usually means rain or snow.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p14",
      "text": "So pay attention to the signs.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p15",
      "text": "If rainbows form in the west at sunrise, the sun is on the way.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p16",
      "text": "Smell the flowers, their smells are stronger in wet air.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p17",
      "text": "What are the ants doing?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p18",
      "text": "Are they moving to higher ground?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p19",
      "text": "This could mean a drop in air pressure.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p20",
      "text": "Are the birds flying low or high?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p21",
      "text": "Falling air pressure may influence birds ears, so they fly low.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s42-p22",
      "text": "And if the sky is red at sunset, you might plan a picnic for the next day.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p22.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s42-p22.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
